name: Exact relationship selection and grouping across two Git revisions
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE NODE_OPTIONS NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/relationship_book.py @TMP_TARGET @ART prepare
require-wrapper-flow:
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET/owned
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
paste-file: @ART/open-center.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 20 Viewing Review | opened-center
submit: relationships
require-live-snap: 30 50 relationships | first-page
keys: Escape
resize: 40x12
require-live-snap: 20 n/p pages | compact-browser-40x12
expect: n/p pages
expect: R refresh
ask: Can an operator discover paging, refresh and relationship review in the compact browser without treating a duplicate link as a finding verdict?
resize: 120x36
keys: n
require-live-snap: 20 page 2 | second-page
keys: Down Down Down Down Down Down Down Down Down
require-live-snap: 20 Labeled book pair 001 | selected-primary
keys: a
paste-file: @ART/accept-note.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 20 outside this page | accepted-recorded-selection
expect: Accepted
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/relationship_book.py @TMP_TARGET @ART accepted
resize: 160x48
require-live-snap: 20 outside this page | saved-pair-160x48
resize: 96x89
require-live-snap: 20 outside this page | saved-pair-96x89
resize: 80x24
require-live-snap: 20 outside this page | saved-pair-80x24
resize: 60x20
require-live-snap: 20 outside this page | saved-pair-60x20
resize: 40x12
require-live-snap: 20 outside this page | saved-pair-40x12
keys: PageDown
live-snap: saved-details-1-40x12
keys: PageDown
live-snap: saved-details-2-40x12
keys: PageDown
live-snap: saved-details-3-40x12
keys: PageDown
live-snap: saved-details-4-40x12
keys: PageDown
live-snap: saved-details-5-40x12
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/relationship_book.py @TMP_TARGET @ART narrow
ask: Does saving the oldest pair retain that exact accepted revision after it moves off page two, with its recorded IDs, runs and reason reachable at every size?
resize: 120x36
keys: Home
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/relationship_book.py @TMP_TARGET @ART later
keys: R
require-live-snap: 20 outside this page | baseline-pair-after-source-change
keys: Space A
require-live-snap: 20 REVIEW 1 RELATIONSHIPS | recorded-pair-inspection
keys: ] Enter
require-live-snap: 20 G return | recorded-generation
expect: Viewing Review
keys: PageDown
live-snap: recorded-source-page-1
keys: PageDown
live-snap: recorded-source-page-2
keys: PageDown
live-snap: recorded-source-page-3
keys: PageDown
live-snap: recorded-source-page-4
keys: G
require-live-snap: 20 REVIEW 1 RELATIONSHIPS | returned-to-pair
keys: Escape
require-live-snap: 20 FINDING RELATIONSHIPS | returned-browser
keys: Home u
paste-file: @ART/old-unlink-note.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 20 Duplicate · Removed | baseline-unlinked
expect: outside this page
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/relationship_book.py @TMP_TARGET @ART old-unlinked
keys: p
require-live-snap: 20 page 1 | returned-first-page
keys: Down
require-live-snap: 20 Labeled book pair 001 | fresh-pair-selected
expect: Proposed
keys: a
paste-file: @ART/fresh-accept-note.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 20 Reviewed only the fresh pair | fresh-pair-accepted
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/relationship_book.py @TMP_TARGET @ART fresh-accepted
keys: u
paste-file: @ART/fresh-unlink-note.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 20 Unlink only the fresh pair | fresh-pair-unlinked
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/relationship_book.py @TMP_TARGET @ART finished
ask: Can the operator inspect the original recorded generation, unlink only the old pair, and separately accept then unlink a fresh pair without losing observations or inventing fixed status after the SHA change?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME NO_COLOR=1 KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET/owned
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | restarted
paste-file: @ART/open-center.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 20 Viewing Review | recovered-center
submit: relationships
require-live-snap: 20 Removed | recovered-pairs-prompt
keys: Escape
require-live-snap: 20 Removed | recovered-pairs
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/relationship_book.py @TMP_TARGET @ART restarted
ask: Does no-color restart retain both exact historical pair decisions, all 121 observations and usable paging, with no model work or finding-verdict changes?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
